<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Diagram atlas</title>
<style>
__DOTS_THEME_CSS__

.page {
    max-width: var(--article);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 64px 24px 96px;
  }
  .page[data-layout="wide"] { max-width: var(--wide); }
  .page[data-layout="canvas"] { max-width: var(--canvas); }
  .reading-column { max-width: var(--article); }
  .page[data-layout="article"] .reading-column,
  .page[data-layout="wide"] .reading-column { margin-right: auto; }
  .page[data-layout="canvas"] .reading-column { margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; }
  .page > header { margin-bottom: var(--section); }
  .context-line { font-size: 13px; color: var(--text-muted); margin: 0 0 20px; }
  .title-row { margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .dek { font-size: 16px; color: var(--text-muted); margin: 0; max-width: 62ch; }
  footer.sources {
    margin-top: 64px; padding-top: 24px; border-top: 1px solid var(--a12);
    font-size: 12px; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.7;
  }
  footer.sources a { color: var(--text-muted); }
  @media (max-width: 680px) {
    .page { padding: 40px 24px 72px; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div data-component="page-shell" class="page" data-layout="canvas">
  <header class="stagger">
    <p class="context-line">dots html / visual vocabulary</p>
    <div class="title-row">
      <h1>Diagram atlas</h1>

    </div>
    <p class="dek">__DIAGRAM_COUNT__ reusable templates for structure, process, hierarchy, interaction, and quantitative explanation.</p>
  </header>

  __DIAGRAM_STYLES__

  <div class="reading-column diagram-intro">
    <section id="choose">
      <h2>Choose the relationship before drawing</h2>
      <p>These __DIAGRAM_COUNT__ templates cover system structure, process, hierarchy, interaction, and quantitative explanation. Copy the closest figure, keep the shared visual rules, and replace every illustrative label with grounded content.</p>
      <p>Use a table for a binary comparison and prose when the diagram would only put a box around a sentence.</p>
    </section>
  </div>

  __DIAGRAM_FIGURES__
  <div class="reading-column">
    <section id="rules">
      <h2>Shared limits</h2>
      <p>Embedded diagrams target 4–9 nodes and one or two focal elements. Keep equivalent meaning in adjacent HTML, inspect the actual display width, and split a drawing that cannot remain legible without shrinking labels.</p>
    </section>
  </div>

  <footer class="sources">Illustrative templates only. Replace every label and value with grounded source material; the shared Dots identity remains fixed.</footer>
</div>

</body>
</html>
